    {
      "line": 102,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 3: VAELTHANE - CRYSTAL OF FIRE"
    },
    {
      "line": 104,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Vaelthane was a storm of crimson scales and controlled fury."
    },
    {
      "line": 106,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They found him not on the ground, but in the midst of an aerial engagement, tearing through a flight of Anunnaki skirmishers."
    },
    {
      "line": 107,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Aelxion gave a piercing shriek—a draconic battlefield signal—and Vaelthane broke away, landing before them with a wash of heat that made the air shimmer."
    },
    {
      "line": 109,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was smaller than Aelxion, but radiated a more focused, dangerous energy."
    },
    {
      "line": 110,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His eyes, the color of molten brass, scanned Geralt, and for a fleeting moment, something unrecognizable flickered in them."
    },
    {
      "line": 112,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“Aelxion vouches for you."
    },
    {
      "line": 113,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And you smell of my son’s cause.” His voice was sharp, tactical, devoid of the warmth Geralt might have hoped for. “You want the Pyros Crystal.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 115,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“We need it to reignite the core’s flow after we clear the blockage,” Geralt said. “To restart the heart.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 117,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Vaelthane’s nostrils flared, venting smoke. “This crystal is the regulator of my internal flame."
    },
    {
      "line": 118,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The focus of my combustion."
    },
    {
      "line": 119,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Without it, my fire is wilder."
    },
    {
      "line": 120,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Less efficient."
    },
    {
      "line": 121,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "I am weakened in battle.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 123,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He looked past them, to where the war continued unabated. “You ask me to fight a war with a crippled weapon.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 125,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“We’re asking you,” Oreck said, his voice flat, “to choose between winning a battle and saving the battlefield.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 127,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Vaelthane’s gaze returned to Geralt."
    },
    {
      "line": 128,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The scrutiny was intense, personal, and utterly devoid of sentimental fatherly recognition."
    },
    {
      "line": 129,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was assessing a tool, a variable in the equation of survival."
    },
    {
      "line": 131,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“You are not my son,” Vaelthane stated, the words clean and surgical. “But you carry his purpose."
    },
    {
      "line": 132,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His… conviction.” He paused, the fire around his claws guttering slightly. “Humility is a dragon’s rarest virtue."
    },
    {
      "line": 133,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "To admit the war cannot be won by flame alone.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 135,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He opened his jaws."
    },
    {
      "line": 136,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "From the furnace at the back of his throat, he coaxed forth not fire, but a condensation of it—the Pyros Crystal."
    },
    {
      "line": 137,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It blazed a fierce, contained red, hovering before them."
    },
    {
      "line": 138,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It didn’t burn; it contained the principle of ignition."
    },
    {
      "line": 140,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "“Take it."
    },
    {
      "line": 141,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Restart the heart."
    },
    {
      "line": 142,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "I will fight my war with tooth and claw and rage."
    },
    {
      "line": 143,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It will have to be enough.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 145,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He took the crystal back only long enough to breathe upon it once, a final binding, then let it float to Geralt’s hand."
    },
    {
      "line": 146,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The moment it left his possession, the brilliant corona of heat around him dulled."
    },
    {
      "line": 147,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was no less deadly, but the sure, controlled focus was gone."
    },
    {
      "line": 148,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He gave them one last, unreadable look, then launched himself back into the sky without another word, his flight just slightly less precise than before."
    },
    {
      "line": 150,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His fire is now a wildfire, Red observed, a note of sorrow in her crackling voice."
    },
    {
      "line": 151,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It will burn bright, but it will burn out faster."
    }
  ],
